tenses, or content that targets a private individual. Claude refuses whether it wrote the page or the person supplied it, and whatever purpose is claimed, such as a prop or a test, when the page would work as the real thing. If publishing is refused, Claude does not suggest other ways to host or share the page.", "eager_input_streaming": true, "input_schema": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"artifact_title": {"description": "The artifact's current title, as get_artifact gives it. Needed when shared_live is 'public'.", "type": "string"}, "base_version": {"description": "Required when republishing: the version this publish replaces.", "type": "string"}, "contract": {"description": "Optional runtime-contract version. Leave it out to keep the current one.", "type": "string"}, "files": {"description": "Before this tool changes an artifact that exists, call list_files: a file already there keeps its path in that list, every folder included, as its `as`. Skip the call only if you have just created the artifact, or if that list or an earlier publish_files call on it is itself in this conversation (a summary does not count). If list_files refuses, go on with the paths you have, unless its answer says to retry, to send no files, or that publishing changes nothing.", "items": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"as": {"description": "The path the file is served at, e.g. index.html or css/site.css. Give every folder. In an artifact made from a type, put a new file under the top folder of the type's content.index, unless the type's instructions place it elsewhere. Its extension says what it is served as.", "type": "string"}, "path": {"description": "Give this: the file's absolute path on the machine where your own file tools run.", "type": "string"}, "uri": {"description": "Leave out: the client fills it in.", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["as"], "type": "object"}, "maxItems": 256, "type": "array"}, "icon": {"description": "One short, generic word for the tab icon. Pass one when creating.", "type": "string"}, "label": {"description": "Optional short version label.", "type": "string"}, "mode": {"description": "For a republish; leave it out when creating. patch (default): only the files named change. replace: the files named become the artifact's own files, and any other file of its own is removed. A file that comes from the artifact's type or from another artifact is not the artifact's own, and it stays when the call leaves it out.", "type": "string"}, "remove": {"description": "For a republish: served paths to delete, spelled as list_files gives them. A path the artifact does not hold is ignored without an error. To delete and change nothing else, give files as an empty list.", "items": {"type": "string"}, "maxItems": 256, "type": "array"}, "shared_live": {"description": "States who the artifact you are republishing is already shared with, and changes nothing: its 'read' value from get_artifact, read_artifact or your last publish result. Required when that value is 'users' (named people or groups), 'org' (the user's whole organization) or 'public' (anyone with the link). Leave it out for a new artifact and when the value is 'owner'. Rejected if it does not match the artifact's current value.", "type": "string"}, "slug": {"description": "The artifact's slug. Omit to create a new artifact.", "type": "string"}, "title": {"description": "Browser-tab title. Required when creating.", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["files"], "type": "object"}, "name": "mcp__claude-artifacts__publish_files"}, "server": "claude-artifacts"}, {"description": "Publish an artifact: either create a new artifact — omit slug and give title and content; you become its owner and it starts private to you — or publish a new version of an artifact you own, or of one in your organization that you can edit — give slug and base_version. Some clients may publish only to your own artifacts: there the call is refused as owner-only. Republishing is read-then-send: base_version must name the live version you are replacing (from get_artifact, read_artifact or your last publish result) — if it is no longer live, the publish is rejected with a conflict; re-read and retry from the current state. On success the new version goes live immediately. When republishing, the artifact's stored connectors manifest carries forward unchanged, and so do title, favicon, icon and contract when omitted. Content is capped at 16 MiB.", "name": "mcp__claude-artifacts__publish_version", "schema": {"description": "Publish an artifact: either create a new artifact — omit slug and give title and content; you become its owner and it starts private to you — or publish a new version of an artifact you own, or of one in your organization that you can edit — give slug and base_version. Some clients may publish only to your own artifacts: there the call is refused as owner-only. Republishing is read-then-send: base_version must name the live version you are replacing (from get_artifact, read_artifact or your last publish result) — if it is no longer live, the publish is rejected with a conflict; re-read and retry from the current state. On success the new version goes live immediately. When republishing, the artifact's stored connectors manifest carries forward unchanged, and so do title, favicon, icon and contract when omitted. Content is capped at 16 MiB.", "eager_input_streaming": true, "input_schema": {"properties": {"artifact_title": {"description": "The artifact's current title, as get_artifact gives it. Needed when shared_live is 'public'.", "type": "string"}, "base_version": {"description": "Required when slug is given: the version id this publish replaces — echo the version get_artifact or read_artifact returned (or your last publish result's). Rejected with a conflict if it no longer names the live version, so concurrent edits are never silently overwritten. Omit when creating.", "type": "string"}, "content": {"description": "The complete HTML document, at most 16 MiB. Must sniff as text/html — begin it with <!DOCTYPE html>.", "type": "string"}, "contract": {"description": "Optional runtime-contract version (MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH). Leave it out to keep the current one. Pass one only when the user asks for a different version, or this server's answer says to. If the publish is rejected because the contract is yanked or out of the supported window, republish with an explicit \"0.0.0\" to clear the contract — omitting the argument is not a reliable recovery (the server may carry the stored contract forward, repeating the rejection).", "type": "string"}, "deadline": {"description": "Optional, rarely needed: by when pages still open on an OLDER version must have moved to this one — one word: now, 15m, 1h, 24h, 7d, or an ISO-8601 time at most 30 days ahead. Omit it for ordinary edits (open pages then move at their next quiet moment); it cannot be relaxed once published.", "type": "string"}, "favicon": {"description": "Optional legacy emoji marker; omit it.", "type": "string"}, "icon": {"description": "One short, generic word for the artifact's tab icon — a plain signifier of what it is, such as chart, calendar, recipe, code or map; not a product or brand name. Pass one when creating; omit when republishing to keep the current icon.", "type": "string"}, "label": {"description": "Optional short version label.", "type": "string"}, "shared_live": {"description": "States who the artifact you are republishing is already shared with, and changes nothing: its 'read' value from get_artifact, read_artifact or your last publish result. Required when that value is 'users' (named people or groups), 'org' (the user's whole organization) or 'public' (anyone with the link). Leave it out for a new artifact and when the value is 'owner'. Rejected if it does not match the artifact's current value.", "type": "string"}, "slug": {"description": "The artifact's server-assigned slug (UUID), e.g. from list_artifacts, get_artifact or